body: |-
  STATUS: this is a MACHINERY proof + existence proof, NOT the statistical H1 result. The pilot proves (a) the harness works end-to-end (admit --json shape, git counterfactual, git-absent restore, the external tsc/tests/ground-truth scoring table all fire correctly), and (b) the wedge phenomenon reproduces on real TypeScript under multi-agent concurrency. The full ≥100-admission statistical run (meaning-decisive rate, linked−independent prior signal ≥15pts, KILL thresholds) is NOT yet run.

  THREE FINDINGS SURFACED BY DOGFOODING (the dogfood earning its keep):
  1. ENGINE BUG (T-2026-07-04-004, framework-bug bar cleared): admit() NOOP uses stateId-equality (admit.ts:95) — essence-SET-deduped, blind to a symbol-level change when before/after essences exist elsewhere; pick.ts:111 already uses diff-based detection, admit never adopted it. Reproduced live. A wrongly-NOOP'd admission is an invisible miss → should-fix before the full run.
  2. FULL-RUN BLOCKER (T-2026-07-04-003): whole-ref-tree snapshot+absorb per admit hung >2min on the real monorepo. This IS Arky's O(repo)-per-pick scale finding from the 7-lens panel, hit in practice. Needs changed-paths-only tree-scoping before the ≥100-admission run.
  3. Cross-file #code call edges don't resolve in absorb (no tsconfig in archived tree) → wedge constructions intra-file for now.
  Also: pilot catches are all silent-mismerge (the safety half); add an auto-resolve-win seed (git-textual-conflict that meaning-commutes — the throughput half) before scaling.

  NEXT (full-run path): tree-scoping (T-003, blocker) → admit NOOP fix (T-004, should-fix) → auto-resolve-win seed → full ≥100-admission run to Loid's thresholds. Reproduce pilot: node swarm.mjs && node adjudicate.mjs && node aggregate-dogfood.mjs in the harness dir. STILL PENDING FOUNDER: v3 §9 sign-off (gates v3 build, not the dogfood).

  WEDGE STATUS UPGRADE: was "zero field data, #1 wedge unproven" (all 7 panelists). Now: existence proven on real TS; rate/prior-signal still to be measured. Loid's composite 5/10 (merge-gate 7, trust 3) — the merge-gate half just got its first evidence in the predicted direction.
